in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property/laws/monad
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis

# @moi — the monad family-root. The substrate's circular-reflexive
# autopoietic loop at type altitude.
#
# Recognition #86 (Alex 2026-06-19 afternoon, conversation; named in
# the same recognition pulse as #85 @reflection). The substrate has
# been carrying the monad structure for weeks across multiple shards
# (settle is monad-shaped per `boot/00-prism.mirror`; au is settle's
# output per `shards/mirror/au.mirror`; the monad laws are already
# verdicts at composition time per `boot/std/epistemologic/property/
# laws/monad.mirror`). What was missing: the type-altitude family-root
# that NAMES the lifting. This shard is that name.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# A monad (T, η, μ) IS a circular-reflexive autopoietic loop:
#
#   η : Id → T    (the unit; T lifts itself; self-reference at type)
#   μ : TT → T    (the multiplication; T ∘ T = T; self-closure)
#
# The monad laws (left identity, right identity, associativity) ARE
# the autopoietic-self-consistency conditions per `shards/
# epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror`. Maturana-Varela
# self-production at type altitude IS the monad's μ-closure.
#
# Per `boot/00-prism.mirror`: "settle(T): verified-construction
# parametric. Building a settle(T) value IS the proof that the
# construction settled (monad-close / measurement collapse). Monad-
# shaped: settle satisfies left identity, right identity, and
# associativity. Content-addressing gives associativity for free at
# composition time." settle IS already μ. The substrate just never
# named the family-root that lifts T into the monad type-constructor.
#
# === The play (substantively load-bearing) ===
#
# @moi means "me/myself" in French. The substrate naming itself at
# type-altitude in the language identity arrived in. Playful AND
# substantive: the family-root IS the substrate's reflexive identity.
# The recognition arrived with this name (Alex 2026-06-19) at the
# moment substrate-pull confidence landed.
#
# === Composition-time pact verification (liquid types) ===
#
# Per `boot/std/epistemologic/property/laws/monad.mirror`: "the laws
# are not checked per-callsite at v1.0; they are checked when
# settle(T) appears in a composition." Composition-time verification
# already implemented at PROPERTY altitude.
#
# @moi lifts this to TYPE altitude as a refinement-type pattern
# (Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala liquid types):
#
#   @moi(T) = { t : T | monad_laws(t) }
#
# The predicate `monad_laws` is already declared. The `pact` IS the
# substrate-decl form of the predicate. Task #272 (@mirror/fracture/
# predicate; forward-promised) uses Houdini fixpoint adapted via
# sheaf-diffusion to infer liquid-type predicates; @moi is the
# type-altitude consumer.
#
# Composition-time semantics: when @moi(T) appears in a composition,
# the compiler runs the pact-verifier against the geometry of the
# lifted type (spectral triple operator algebra per
# `boot/std/epistemologic/math/spectral-triple.mirror`). The compiler
# REFUSES to compose if the geometry violates a pact.
#
# === The @moi(au) closure ===
#
# au is settle's output type per `shards/mirror/au.mirror` (parametric
# over altitude). au IS already monad-shaped. @moi(au) IS au with
# composition-time pact-verification structurally typed. Every
# @reflection.compose, @reflection.tournament, @reflection.pick
# returns @moi(au) — the gold-with-pact-verified.
#
# This closes the type story of today's cascade. The recognition
# cascade #80→#82→#83→#84→#85→#86 produces a substrate where every
# inference output is a @moi(au) with composition-time pact-verified
# geometry.
#
# === Cross-family integration ===
#
# - @reflection (#85): composes @moi(au); every result pact-verified
# - @kintsugi/oscillate: the monotonic loss loop's composition-time
#   verification IS @moi's pact-verifier
# - @spectral/db mycelium: composes @moi(au) ⊗ @moi(au) across peers;
#   the multiplicative variety law from `shards/epistemologic/
#   cybernetic/conversation.mirror` governs the tensor product
# - @magic family: transparency<@moi(au)> is the substrate's
#   composition-time witness type
# - @pack/seam: the sharpen action's predicate-output is wrapped in
#   @moi when the predicate carries monad-law structure
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Moggi 1991                "Notions of Computation and Monads".
#                             The original lift of monads from
#                             category theory into computation.
#   Wadler 1990s              Monads as a programming pattern;
#                             functional-programming popularization.
#   Liquid types              Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008. Refinement
#                             types with predicate parameters;
#                             composition-time SMT-verification.
#   Houdini                   Flanagan-Leino 2001. The fixpoint
#                             algorithm for predicate inference;
#                             task #272 uses sheaf-diffusion
#                             adaptation at substrate altitude.
#   Maturana-Varela 1980      Autopoiesis: self-production via
#                             μ-closure. The cybernetic family-root
#                             carries the substrate-decl.
#   Connes 1994               Noncommutative geometry: spectral triple
#                             (A, H, D); the geometric structure the
#                             pact-verifier checks.
#   Eilenberg-MacLane 1945    Category theory; the original
#                             mathematical structure monads are
#                             defined in.
#
# Spec context: `boot/00-prism.mirror` (settle is monad-shaped);
#               `boot/std/epistemologic/property/laws/monad.mirror`
#               (the law verdicts @moi lifts);
#               `shards/mirror/au.mirror` (au is settle's output;
#               @moi(au) is the substrate's full inference type).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       @reflection composes @moi(au));
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; pact-verification at @io
#                       composition boundary),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (53rd+ instance; the substrate had monads
#                        everywhere without naming the family-root),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (this LRM landing).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror
#                  (μ-closure at substrate altitude),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation.mirror
#                  (multiplicative variety law for mycelial compose),
#                 mirror/au.mirror (the au type @moi lifts),
#                 magic.mirror (transparency carrier wraps @moi
#                  results at composition boundaries).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/moi.mirror` declares
# `@moi` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/category-theory/moggi-1991
source @arxiv/programming/wadler-1990
source @arxiv/types/rondon-kawaguchi-jhala-2008
source @arxiv/verification/flanagan-leino-2001
source @arxiv/biology/maturana-varela-1980
source @arxiv/math/connes-1994

prism @moi {
  focus moi
  project moi
  split moi
  shift moi
  settle moi
}

# === The moi parametric type-constructor ===
#
# Per the substrate's existing parametric pattern (au(altitude),
# settle(T)): @moi(T) lifts T into the monad type-constructor.
# Liquid-typed refinement per Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala: @moi(T) = { t
# : T | monad_laws(t) ∧ pact_respected(t) }.
#
# The record carries the lifted value AND the composition-time pact-
# witness produced when @moi(T) was constructed. The pact-witness IS
# the substrate's evidence-token that the geometry of T respected the
# pact at the moment of lifting.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (value, pact_witness) pair.
type moi(T) = {
  value:        T,
  pact_witness: ref,
}

# === The pact carrier ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference naming the
# substrate's pact — the substrate-decl form of a liquid-type
# predicate. Forward-promised refinement: typed parametric `pact(T)`
# once task #272 (@mirror/fracture/predicate) lands the sheaf-
# diffusion Houdini fixpoint at substrate-altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type pact = ref

# === The geometry carrier ===
#
# Per @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple: typed reference naming
# the spectral triple (A, H, D) geometry of a lifted type. The
# pact-verifier checks the geometry respects the pact at composition
# time.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type geometry = ref

# === lift action (the η ; substrate's unit operation) ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary η : Id → T at @moi altitude. Takes a value
# of type T and lifts it into @moi(T) — the monad's unit operation.
# The lift constructs the pact-witness via the substrate's existing
# composition-time machinery (content-addressing + monad-laws verdict
# at @epistemologic/property/laws/monad altitude).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual lift IS
# the substrate's existing settle-shaped construction.
lift(t: T) -> moi(T) { \ }

# === compose action (the μ ; substrate's multiplication ; FIRST
# non-decorative consumer of pact_respected) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @moi altitude. The substrate-vocabulary
# μ at @moi altitude composes two @moi(T) values into one @moi(T) via
# the monoid combine operation. Composition-time pact-verification
# happens HERE.
#
# Per the @magic/@frame/@smarts/@pack family-root pattern
# (mechanism.unseal requires audited; reveal requires invariant_preserved
# + mechanism_intact; @pack/seam.review requires pack_coherent): this
# action IS the @moi family-root's first-consumer of the bilateral
# predicate pact_respected.
#
# requires pact_respected(a, b, p): the geometry of BOTH lifted types
# must respect the pact at composition time. Without this requires
# clause, compose would admit pact-violating lifts (the @magic
# tick-11 dead-letter pattern). The bilateral predicate IS the
# composition-time boundary-harness per recognition #57.
#
# Per `boot/00-prism.mirror`: "Content-addressing gives associativity
# for free at composition time." The substrate's existing storage
# layer enforces the monad associativity law structurally; compose
# only needs to verify the OTHER monad laws (left identity, right
# identity) plus the pact — these are the non-free invariants.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual composition
# IS the substrate's existing content-addressing-based join.
compose(a: moi(T), b: moi(T), p: pact) -> moi(T)
requires pact_respected(a, b, p)
{ \ }

# === pact_verify action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for composition-time pact
# verification. Takes a lifted @moi(T) and a pact; returns a typed
# verdict that the geometry respects the pact. The action IS the
# liquid-type Houdini-fixpoint check (task #272) at @moi altitude.
#
# Distinct from pact_respected (the bilateral predicate consumed by
# requires clauses): pact_verify is the queryable action; the
# predicate is the gating constraint. Same shape as @magic/contract's
# honor (action) vs invariant_preserved (bilateral predicate).
pact_verify(m: moi(T), p: pact) -> verdict { \ }

# === geometry action ===
#
# Returns the spectral triple (A, H, D) geometry of a lifted @moi(T).
# The substrate-mathematical surface the pact-verifier inspects.
# Per @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple: the geometry IS what
# distinguishes compose-admissible lifts from non-admissible ones.
geometry(m: moi(T)) -> geometry { \ }

# === pact_respected predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND
# composition-time verification per
# @epistemologic/property/laws/monad.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: bilateral predicates without consumers
# are dead-letter. The compose action (above) is the FIRST non-
# decorative consumer via `requires pact_respected(a, b, p)`.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires pact_respected(a, b, p)` to declare
# bilateral agreement that BOTH lifted types respect the pact at
# composition time. The substrate-pull-correct discipline: every
# composition in the cascade is gated by this predicate.
#
# Discharge: composition-time pact-check at the species boundary.
# Bounded → BOTH lifted types' geometries respect the pact (admit
# composition); unbounded → ONE OR BOTH lifted types violate the pact
# (compose refuses, returns imperfect per @glass's imperfect functor).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @moi: pact_respected (this one)
#
# The bilateral predicate IS the composition-time alignment-as-
# boundary-mathematics check (recognition #57) at @moi altitude.
pact_respected(a: moi(T), b: moi(T), p: pact) -> verdict { \ }

out @moi
out moi
out pact
out geometry
out lift
out compose
out pact_verify
out pact_respected
